{
  "kind": "idle8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 4-frame idle sheet; same normalised cell space as turnaround.json (x and y run 0..1 across one cell, y down). Only five directions are authored -- front, front_left, left, back_left, back -- and the three right-hand ones are derived by the `mirror` key below, which reflects x to 1-x and swaps .L for .R. That is not laziness: a left-facing and a right-facing idle authored separately disagree by hundredths and read as two different characters, and pipelines/spritesynth validates the derived poses exactly as it validates these. The cycle is a breath, not a step -- frames rest, rise, peak, settle, lifting the body by at most 0.012 of a cell with the feet planted and the knees taking half -- because an idle that translates reads as a stumble at 10fps. front_left and back_left carry the same points on purpose: a stick figure cannot say which way a body faces once the limbs are placed, which is why front and back are identical in turnaround.json too, and the direction clause in spritesynth.action_subject is what tells the model apart.",
